WEBVTT
Language: en

seg-001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
Welcome to this short sample lesson.

seg-002
00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:08.209
Today you will learn what a variable is
in Python.

seg-003
00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:11.680
A variable is a name that holds a value.

seg-004
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.270
Think of it as a labelled box.

seg-005
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.509
First write the name,
then an equals sign, then the value.

seg-006
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.470
For example, name equals Abebe.

seg-007
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.750
Now the box called name
holds the word Abebe.

seg-008
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.150
You can change what is inside at any time.

seg-009
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.530
Write age equals twenty,
then age equals twenty-one.

seg-010
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.880
The box keeps only the newest value.

seg-011
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.950
To see what is inside,
use the print command.

seg-012
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.640
Printing name shows Abebe on the screen.

seg-013
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.490
Good names make code easier to read.

seg-014
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.000
Use clear words like price or total,
not single letters.

seg-015
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:04.030
Let us practise. Create a variable called
city, give it your city, and print it.

seg-016
00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:07.899
Well done. You have written
your first variable.
